From 66b5f8d266d7cb92576f30ec5b02ecff17fb6e22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 12:01:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] U1: Unknown-way transfer Maker-Checker workflow

Unknown-way transfer lines no longer settle immediately at creation or
branch-request confirm. They now follow the same create -> pending ->
settle lifecycle Known-way lines already had:

- TransferComposer.StageAsync: Unknown-way lines move source
  Available -> Hold at create time (mirroring Known-way exactly, minus
  item selection) and leave the target untouched. Every line, Known or
  Unknown, is staged pending; the transfer always opens InProgress.
- TransferService.SettleAsync: Unknown-way lines are now real openLines.
  A remainder requires an explicit CardTransferProduct.DifferenceAction
  (ReturnedToSource spawns an auto-generated return transfer exactly
  like the Known-way path; KeptAtDestination credits the target's
  Available in full and spawns nothing). Disposal is rejected for
  Unknown-way (no physical card to write off).
- Maker/Checker identity: CardTransfer.CreatedByUsername (required) and
  .CheckedByUsername (nullable, set at settlement) record the acting
  account on every transfer. Per the repo owner: it is fine for the
  same account to be both Maker and Checker (this system has one
  account per tenant, so there is no per-user identity to compare) -
  what matters is that identity is recorded.
- BranchRequestService.ConfirmAsync / BranchRequestFulfilment: an
  Unknown-way line confirmed via a branch request no longer credits
  ReceivedQuantity inline - BranchRequestFulfilment.ApplyReceiptAsync
  is now the single credit path for every settled line, Known or
  Unknown, applied identically per the repo owner's confirmation.
- New: TransferDifferenceAction enum, four TransferErrors entries
  (DifferenceActionRequired/NotApplicable, InvalidDifferenceAction,
  DisposalNotAllowedForUnknown), EN/AR localization, migration
  U1-UnknownTransferMakerChecker.
- Corrected two stale doc comments (CardTransferItem entity, and this
  project's own PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE.md) that incorrectly claimed
  Unknown-way lines get CardTransferItem rows - they never have.

Verification note: no .NET SDK / NuGet access in the working sandbox
for this pass - verified by careful manual re-read of every edited
file and call site, not the usual Roslyn semantic compile. Recommend
a real build before merging.
